@startuml c6-sequence
' DOC-9. C6, the solver: how an analysis asks and what it gets back.
' Card: docs/algorithms/C6.md#pseudocode
' code: flowstat.analysis.guards:analyse
' code: flowstat.solver.solve:overlap
' code: flowstat.solver.solve:uncovered
' code: flowstat.solver.solve:check
' code: flowstat.solver.predicate:dnf
' code: flowstat.solver.diffgraph:solve_differences
skinparam shadowing false

participant "guards.analyse" as guards
participant "overlap, uncovered" as ask
participant "check" as check
participant "dnf" as dnf
participant "_solve_clause" as clause
participant "solve_differences" as bf

guards -> ask : guards of a branch group, domains
ask -> check : And(p, q) or And(Not p...)
check -> dnf : nnf(pred), cap
dnf --> check : clauses, or None
loop every clause
  check -> clause : clause, domains
  clause -> bf : difference edges (when two variables meet)
  bf --> clause : values, or a negative cycle
  clause --> check : sat with a witness, unsat, or unknown
end
check --> ask : sat (a case), unsat (a proof), unknown
ask --> guards : a finding with a case, or none
@enduml
